# Testing core rules (binding)

Design: `testing/docs/TESTING_ARCHITECTURE.md`. Tasks: `testing/docs/IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md`.
Service facts (routes, DI seams, env vars): `testing/docs/SUT_MAP.md`. **Read SUT_MAP before touching a service. Never re-read the whole repo.**
Python style: `python-style.mdc` (auto). Playwright: `playwright.mdc` (auto in UI dirs).

## 0. Scope and behaviour
- Write only in: `testing/`, `.github/workflows/`, `infra/docker-compose.test.yml`, `infra/nginx/nginx.test.conf`, root `Makefile` (include `testing/testing.mk`).
- **Production code:** small behaviour-neutral testability changes are allowed and preferred over fragile test-side hacks, under `testing-modify-prod.mdc`. Never change behaviour or fix bugs here: behaviour that contradicts the documented spec is `xfail(strict=True, reason="BUG-n: ...")` + a line in `testing/KNOWN_ISSUES.md`; unspecified behaviour is pinned with a `# characterization` comment.
- Ignore Datadog everywhere (will be removed).
- Characterise actual behaviour first (read the route, call it), then assert it. Never invent endpoints, fields or status codes; if SUT_MAP lacks it, read that one file.
- Output discipline: no explanations, final report <= 10 lines, no re-printing files. Run the DoD command; on failure show only the last 40 lines.
- One task per chat. Stop when the task's Definition of Done is green.

## 1. Layers (never mix)
| Layer | App | Infra | Tools | Dir |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| unit | none | none | pytest, pytest-mock | `tests/unit` (saas_testkit self-tests now; services later) |
| contract | in-process | PG | OpenAPI validator, Schemathesis, Pydantic, snapshots | `tests/contract/{http,events}` |
| component | in-process ASGI, one service | real PG + Redis + Redpanda | httpx.ASGITransport, respx, mocker.patch | `tests/component/<service>/` |
| integration | real containers (compose) | full stack | httpx (network), Kafka/Redis/MailHog/WireMock clients | `tests/integration/{services,scenarios}` |
| e2e_ui | real containers | full stack | sync Playwright | `tests/e2e_ui/` |
| smoke | fresh stack/staging/prod URL | none | httpx | `tests/smoke/` (post-deploy gate, broad, blocks) |
| synthetic | prod/staging URL | none | httpx (+ sync Playwright for `browser/`) | `tests/synthetic/{api,browser}/` (continuous, narrow, alerts) |
- Markers are applied from the directory by root `conftest.py`; `--strict-markers` is on. Extra markers: `slow`, `chaos`, `db`, `redis`, `kafka`, `serial`, `smoke` (tests/smoke only), `synthetic`, `critical` (fast UI subset).
- **One service per pytest session** (controller + its xdist workers, all OS processes) for component/contract (all services are named `app`): run with `--service <name>`.
- Tests contain only business-language steps via Flows / Page Objects. No URLs, headers, SQL, locators or raw JSON in test bodies. **The assertion about the behaviour under test stays visible in the test body**; flows return `ApiResponse` for it. Precondition steps (`new_task`) may assert inside flows.
- Protocols only when a boundary has >= 2 implementations (none at start). Adapters (`HttpTaskApi`, `HttpAuthApi`, `KafkaEventReader`) are concrete classes; the same Flow runs at component and integration level because only the injected `httpx.AsyncClient` transport differs. Dependency failures are injected with `mocker.patch(autospec=True)`.

- Smoke and synthetic reuse flows/adapters but differ in policy: smoke blocks a pipeline; synthetic alerts after 3 consecutive failures. Synthetic tests use a dedicated user, `X-Synthetic: true`, `synthetic-` data, per-step latency budgets (soft warn / hard fail), are non-destructive and read `SYNTHETIC_BASE_URL`.

## 2. Data and isolation
- All test data is unique via `RunContext(run_id, test_id)` (`unique_title()`). **Never assert on totals/emptiness of shared collections** (e.g. `GET /tasks`); assert on your own ids.
- Component: DB per xdist worker from a migrated template DB, **real commits**, the app builds its own engine from env (no `get_db` override). Redis: one DB index per worker (env), `FLUSHDB` before each test. Kafka: real Redpanda, unique ids + fresh consumer group, filter by own correlation id.
- Default is no DB cleanup (unique data). Tests that assert on global state use `@pytest.mark.clean_db` (truncates only tables touched since the last cleanup, before the test body).
- Integration/UI: no cleanup/reset. Own data by uuid. Seeded users are read-only. Login and seed **once per run** (FileLock, token file with expiry check), never per test. Nginx `/auth/` allows 5 req/min and is never relaxed; functional tests use the gateway port, real nginx only for UI and edge tests. WireMock stubs are matched on the test's own `payload.id`.
- Factories: **Polyfactory** (Faker bundled), shared by all layers. `.build()` = no I/O (unit, contract, API payloads, envelopes). `await .create_async()` = DB rows via a per-test bound `__async_session__` (the `rows` fixture); `.create_sync()` = sync seeding (FileLock) or sync setup against the stack. Bind the session via a per-test subclass, never a mutable shared class attribute or ContextVar. Override business-constrained fields explicitly; seed with `Factory.seed_random(run_seed)`. Cache one argon2 hash; never hash per test.
- Tests are order-independent and parallel-safe (`pytest-randomly` + xdist). Heavy shared resources are session-scoped and created by the xdist controller only.

## 3. Fixtures, async, mocking
- Scopes: infra = session; engine/clients = session (per worker); db session/app overrides = function. Always `yield` + cleanup; always `dependency_overrides.clear()` in teardown.
- pytest-asyncio: `asyncio_mode="auto"`; default fixture AND test loop scope = `session`.
- No `TestClient` with async DB. Use `httpx.AsyncClient(transport=ASGITransport(app))`. ASGITransport does not run lifespan: enter `app.router.lifespan_context(app)` in a session fixture if needed.
- `respx` = intercept our outgoing httpx calls in-process. `WireMock` = real network stub for scripted sequences (503,503,200), timeouts, request journal. Do not use both for the same call.
- Eventual consistency: `await eventually(fn, timeout=..., interval=..., message=...)`. Kafka test consumers: unique `group_id`, subscribe before producing, filter by own correlation id.
- Retry/backoff tests: patch `asyncio.sleep` and jitter; assert the call sequence, not wall-clock time.

## 4. Quality gates (before "done")
`ruff check`, `ruff format --check`, `pyright` (strict on `src/saas_testkit/`), `pytest <layer> -q` pass; no unknown-marker warnings; tests pass 3x in a row with random order and `-n auto`.
Naming: `test_<behaviour>_<condition>_<expected>`; one behaviour per test; parametrize instead of copy-paste.
After writing tests for a service, spot-check that they can fail: break one line of prod code (or flip one assertion) and confirm a test goes red, then revert.
